Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a Topology Response to the agent's radio waiting for it

The controller gave an agent's Topology Response (like its AP Capability and Channel Preference
Reports) to the em of the agent's first radio. Only an em in topology sync takes the response:
after a radio other than the first was renewed alone, the agent answered every Topology Query
but the first radio's em, already synchronized, ignored the answers, the renewed radio's
em_config waited out its time limit (about 45 s) and the controller renewed every radio of the
agent ("Topology sync did not complete within TTL"), once in a burst of renews. The response now
goes to the agent's radio in topology sync, if one is, else to the first radio as before (steady
state). The AP Capability and Channel Preference Reports are taken by any of the agent's ems
and complete every radio waiting for them: unchanged.

Platform-independent.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/ctrl/em_ctrl.cpp b/src/ctrl/em_ctrl.cpp
index 3c78af7..f108e56 100644
--- a/src/ctrl/em_ctrl.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/em_ctrl.cpp
@@ -1366,6 +1366,22 @@ em_t *em_ctrl_t::find_em_for_msg_type(unsigned char *data, unsigned int len, em_
             }
             if (em == NULL) {
                 em_printfout("No EM found for agent AL MAC %s", util::mac_to_string(hdr->src).c_str());
+            } else if (msg_type == em_msg_type_topo_resp) {
+                // A Topology Response completes the topology sync of the agent's radio waiting
+                // for it (em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending), and only that em takes it: a radio
+                // renewed alone, not the agent's first, waited out its time limit and the
+                // controller renewed every radio of the agent. Without such a radio (steady
+                // state) the first radio takes it, as before. (The AP Capability and Channel
+                // Preference Reports are taken by any of the agent's ems and complete every
+                // radio waiting for them.)
+                for (i = 0; i < dm->get_num_radios(); i++) {
+                    dm_easy_mesh_t::macbytes_to_string(dm->get_radio_info(i)->id.ruid, mac_str1);
+                    em_t *waiting = static_cast<em_t *>(hash_map_get(m_em_map, mac_str1));
+                    if ((waiting != NULL) && (waiting->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_topo_sync_pending)) {
+                        em = waiting;
+                        break;
+                    }
+                }
             }
             break;
 
